<h1>Support</h1>
<p class="lede">Answers to common questions about Cairn. Can't find yours? Email
  <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a>.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>Which phones does Cairn work on?</h3>
  <p class="note">Cairn is coming soon to Android and iPhone.</p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>Is Cairn free?</h3>
  <p class="note">Running your own Cairn server is always free: the code is open source,
    and you only pay for wherever you host it. The hosted server at cairn.cappylabs.uk
    is free to use while Cairn is in development.</p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>Will it drain my battery?</h3>
  <p class="note">Cairn shares on a steady schedule rather than constantly: every
    30 seconds while the app is open, and every 2 minutes in the background. When your
    battery is low and not charging, background sharing slows down (every 5 minutes
    below 35%, every 10 minutes below 15%) and the notification says battery saver is on.
    Background sharing is off unless you turn it on.</p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>What happens if I lose my phone?</h3>
  <p class="note">Your identity is a key that lives on your phone. In the app, open
    <strong>Backup &amp; restore</strong> to save your <strong>24-word recovery phrase</strong>
    somewhere safe; entering it on a new phone brings your identity back.
    We can't recover it for you, because we never have your keys. Without the phrase
    you'd start fresh and pair with people again.</p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>Can CappyLabs see where I am?</h3>
  <p class="note">No. Your location is encrypted on your phone and can only be read by
    the people you've paired with. The server passes it along without being able to
    read it. <a href="/security">Here's exactly what the server can and can't see.</a></p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>How do I stop sharing with someone?</h3>
  <p class="note">Tap them on the map or in your people list. Set sharing to
    <strong>Paused</strong> to stop for now, or remove them to disconnect completely.
    Either way, they stop seeing your location straight away.</p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>I think someone is tracking me with Cairn. What can I do?</h3>
  <p class="note">Open Cairn and check your people list: it shows everyone who can see
    your location. Remove anyone you don't recognise or no longer want to share with.
    If <strong>Share in the background</strong> is on, a notification is always showing;
    turn it off in the sharing settings. If you're in danger, call 999.</p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>How do I delete my data?</h3>
  <p class="note">In the app: menu (⋮) → <strong>Backup &amp; restore</strong> →
    <strong>Delete this identity</strong>. It's immediate. You can also
    <a href="/delete">ask us to delete it</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="card faq">
  <h3>Can I run my own server?</h3>
  <p class="note">Yes. Cairn is open source under the AGPL-3.0. Set up a server with Docker using the
    instructions in the <a href="<%= repo %>">Cairn repository</a>, then in the app go to
    <strong>Settings → Server address</strong>.</p>
</div>

